Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox[
 CounterBox["Section"], "Section"],
 StyleBox[" | Dissipative interactions and open quantum systems", "Section"]
}], "Chapter",
 CounterAssignments->{{"Section", 8}},
 CellID->992917414,ExpressionUUID->"364ee83a-94f8-d54c-b517-d55b71189426"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["The chapter begins by discussing the concept of \
decoherence and dissipation, emphasizing that while the evolution of isolated \
quantum systems is unitary and preserves coherence, real-world systems are \
rarely isolated. We describe the mathematical formalism of open quantum \
systems, the role of the density matrix in describing mixed states, and the \
master equation approach to modeling dissipative dynamics. The chapter also \
explores specific examples, such as the decoherence of superposition states \
(e.g., Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger cat states) and other phenomena that can be \
described by master equations.", "Abstract"]], "Text",
 CellID->457033440,ExpressionUUID->"83e8594d-427d-5144-b684-f6cd3b38bf83"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Key concepts", "Subsubsection"]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9579724558625317`*^9, 3.9579724592668076`*^9}},
 CellID->263168366,ExpressionUUID->"517daa6a-29d7-9241-b6c2-ad3ad73e1b08"],

